#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# min_value

#% text
# `min_value(f, x)` gives the global minimum value of `f`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is the first part of `minimize(f, x)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A parabola:

#% cell
min_value(x^2 + 2*x, x)
#% output
#= -1

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# On an interval:

#% cell
min_value([x^3, -1 <= x and x <= 2], x)
#% output
#= -1

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `minimize` gives the point too:

#% cell
minimize(x^2 + 2*x, x)
#% output
#= [-1, [x -> -1]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `minimize`, `max_value`, `arg_min`
